From 4b2f0b09d907958346ec45301892a297b509ec33 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Thomas Dohmke <thomas@dohmke.de>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] Add fixed (world-anchored) directional shadow boxes

New RenderingServer.light_directional_set_shadow_fixed_box(light, enable, extent, z_near, z_far,
resolution).

A light with a fixed box renders one orthographic map anchored to the light instead of camera-fitted
splits: |x|, |y| <= extent around the light's origin in light space, z_near..z_far along its -Z, the centre
snapped to whole texels in light space (renderer_scene_cull.cpp). Casters are culled to the box and the
light culler uses the camera's far plane as the shadow range. The map is a square of `resolution` pixels
(or the region's shorter side) at the origin of the light's atlas region
(LightStorage::light_directional_get_fixed_box_rect), so a 4096 and a 2048 map can share an 8192 atlas with
their own texel sizes. light_directional_get_shadow_mode() reports ORTHOGONAL for such lights, so the atlas
layout, the light culler and the debug views treat them as one split without further changes.

The map's atlas rectangle goes to the shaders in the DirectionalLightData field that was padding
(uvec2 pad -> shadow_box_rect, two packUnorm2x16 words, zero for other lights), so the struct layout is
unchanged. Forward+, Mobile and the volumetric fog leave receivers outside the box unshadowed
(directional_shadow_box_outside), and the fixed PCF kernel clamps its taps to the map
(directional_shadow_box_clamp_rect). The split distance is 1e30, so there is no split selection and no
distance fade. Renderers without support (Compatibility) keep their camera-fitted maps.

This is the shadow model of SceneKit's automaticallyAdjustsShadowProjection = false (orthographicScale,
zNear, zFar, shadowMapSize) and of most fixed-sun games.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
